  "step_3": "The decision reason requires: (1) a reference value (zero in this case), (2) computation of differences between outcomes and the reference value (i.e., the outcomes themselves), and (3) weighting these differences by their probabilities to compute a mean difference (expected value), then preferring the lottery with the more favorable mean difference. The individual's report does not mention the reference value, nor does it reference any calculation of differences from a reference point. Instead, the individual compares the probabilities and prize amounts in a qualitative, relative manner (5% lower probability, 25% higher prize), without considering expected values or differences from a baseline. Therefore, the individual did not apply the decision reason as defined. The reasoning is qualitatively different and does not reflect the structured comparison of mean differences required by the reason. Hence, the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
