  "step_3": "The decision reason requires: (1) a reference value (zero, since no sure outcome), (2) computing the difference between each outcome and the reference value (i.e., the outcomes themselves), (3) computing the expected value of these differences (i.e., expected loss), and (4) preferring the lottery with the more favorable (i.e., less negative) expected value. The individual's report does not mention the reference value, nor does it compute or refer to expected values. Instead, the individual compares the probability of loss (risk) and the magnitude of loss (25% lower), which is a different kind of reasoning — one that focuses on risk and loss size, not on expected differences from a reference. Therefore, the individual did not apply the decision reason. The information considered (risk and loss magnitude) is not equivalent to the information required by the decision reason (differences from reference value and their weighted expected value). The justification (qualitative comparison of risk and loss size) does not match the rule of the decision reason (expected value of differences from reference). Hence, the decision reason was not used.",
